From: yzddmr6 <46088090+yzddmr6@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] jail: bind the GPU process's library directories read-only

The GPU sandbox only exposes the standard library directories. A host
whose GPU driver lives elsewhere (Xiaomi Pad 8 Pro system 1.2.0 ships
its Adreno 830 Mesa under /opt and lists it in ld.so.conf) therefore
had the sandboxed GPU process fall back to the distribution's Mesa,
which cannot drive that GPU, and render with llvmpipe.

Bind every absolute directory in crosvm's LD_LIBRARY_PATH that is not
already under the standard library directories, read-only, into the GPU
sandbox. Which directories to pass is the launcher's decision; nothing
else in the sandbox changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff --git a/jail/src/helpers.rs b/jail/src/helpers.rs
index 46f5c62..2835fc7 100644
--- a/jail/src/helpers.rs
+++ b/jail/src/helpers.rs
@@ -427,6 +427,21 @@ pub fn create_gpu_minijail(
         ],
     )?;
 
+    // A host graphics stack installed outside those directories (a distribution may ship its GPU
+    // driver under /opt) is found through LD_LIBRARY_PATH. Make those directories visible,
+    // read-only, so the sandboxed GPU process loads the host's driver rather than falling back
+    // to a software renderer.
+    if let Some(paths) = std::env::var_os("LD_LIBRARY_PATH") {
+        for dir in std::env::split_paths(&paths) {
+            let covered = ["/usr/lib", "/usr/lib64", "/lib", "/lib64"]
+                .iter()
+                .any(|root| dir.starts_with(root));
+            if dir.is_absolute() && dir.is_dir() && !covered {
+                jail.mount_bind(&dir, &dir, false)?;
+            }
+        }
+    }
+
     // pvr driver requires read access to /proc/self/task/*/comm.
     mount_proc(&mut jail)?;
 
